pokebw2-worksizes.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): two work sizes in a definition table are the DS
number where the work holds pointers, so on a 64-bit host the work outgrows its block and writes over the next block's
heap header. FIELD_ACTOR_ANM_ASYNC_PROC_TEMPLATE's 0x1a0 (FieldActorAnmProc: 0x1a0 on the DS, 0x1b0 here): the
async proc's work came out of the field heap (HEAPID_FIELDMAP, 21) 16 bytes short, the curve's handle written past it
broke the free block behind it (1.3 MB of the 2.4 MB heap fell off the free list), and the next allocation in the
Route 6 bridge scene (ActorAnimationPlay, zone 331 script 5) found no room: OS_Terminate. BUBBLE_TASK_VTABLE's 0x84
(BubbleTask: 0x84 on the DS, 0x8c here; the underwater bubbles). Each is the work's sizeof, the same number on the DS.
Found with pokebw2-heapreport.patch's BWPORT_HEAPLOG=2 and a scan of the FieldAsyncProcDef, FieldEffectTaskVTable and
WeatherData tables for a number in place of a sizeof (the others have sizeof).

